# What each place of articulation does to the formants, read out of
# enus's own rules. Values are the rules' own integers; `keep' is
# their sentinel for leaving a target unset. `a' is the half before
# the consonant and `b' the half after. Written by
# tools/module/formants.py -- see its head for how the slots were
# identified, which was by measurement and not by any name.
#
# The blocks of a place are tried in the order they appear and the
# first whose conditions all hold is the one that applies.

