# 9 rules, 172 blocks that set a formant value.
#
# `computed' is a value the rule takes from a register rather than
# an immediate -- 33 of the 267 writes -- and this does not resolve
# those. `keep' is the rules' own sentinel for leaving a target
# unset. And the order in which the blocks are tried is read off
# their order in the C and is NOT verified: predicting from it
# disagrees with measurement for /t/ before /i/, where the block
# whose condition names /i/ sets f2b to 1350 and the engine
# measures 1720. So the values here are the rules' own and the
# selection is not to be trusted yet.
